{
 "about": "Historical trade routes (decision 'Playable 8': trade along routes, not a pooled market). Each is a chain of real ports and towns (lon, lat); realms holding places on the same route trade with each other, and realms holding the places between them take a toll on what passes. Routes open in their year (and some close). Places from the Barrington Atlas of the Greek and Roman World (Talbert, 2000) and the standard histories of ancient trade (Young, 'Rome's Eastern Trade', 2001; McLaughlin, 'The Roman Empire and the Indian Ocean', 2014). Our own summary, free for any use.",
